-- do not hand-edit; re-run the generator instead.
--
-- Closes the "has no model defined in creature_template_model" errors for the
-- 260 templates that had no loadable display. The table was never empty -- the
-- core discards model rows whose CreatureDisplayID is missing from
-- CreatureDisplayInfo.dbc, which is the real gap.
--
-- 303 displays are downported from the Cata 4.3.4 client UNDER THEIR ORIGINAL
-- IDS (none collided), so `creature_template_model` needs NO remap.
--
-- Two halves, and BOTH are needed:
--   1. the *_dbc overlay tables below (server: LOAD_DBC merges them at boot)
--   2. the recompiled DBCs in Custom/DBCs, deployed to the client patches AND
--      to the server's data/dbc (the client renders from its own copy)
--
-- creature_model_info is the FOURTH layer and is NOT optional: without a row
-- the creature still refuses to load, with the SAME misleading message -- the
-- failing call is GetCreatureModelRandomGender. Values are inherited from an
-- existing display on the same ModelID rather than defaulted, because bounding
-- radius varies a lot per skeleton (0.208 human female .. 0.8725 tauren).

